# Generated Content

These pseudo‑elements require the `content` property, even if it's empty (`content: ''`). They create a virtual child element that you can style.

```css
.tip::before {
  content: '💡';
  margin-right: 5px;
}
.quote::after {
  content: '”';
}
```
Great for icons, decorative quotes, clearfix hacks, and tooltips. They are inline by default, but you can change display.

slides.codeSnippet:
blockquote {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 30px;
}
blockquote::before {
  content: '“';
  font-size: 4em;
  color: #ccc;
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: -10px;
}

slides.content:
# Style Parts of Text

- `::first-letter` – targets the first character of a block‑level element. Often used for drop caps.
  ```css
  p::first-letter {
    font-size: 2em;
    font-weight: bold;
    float: left;
  }
  ```
- `::first-line` – the first line as rendered by the browser. Dynamic if the container resizes.
- `::selection` – the text the user highlights (colour and background).
  ```css
  ::selection {
    background: gold;
    color: black;
  }
  ```

slides.codeSnippet:
.article p:first-of-type::first-letter {
  font-size: 3em;
  float: left;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-right: 0.1em;
  color: #b22222;
}
::selection {
  background: #ffd700;
}
